mes>PA</given-names></name> (<year>1988</year>) <article-title>A yeast and a human CCAAT-binding protein have heterologous subunits that are functionally interchangeable</article-title>. <source>Cell</source> <volume>53</volume>: <fpage>25</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3280141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>De Vit</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Waddle</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name> (<year>1997</year>) <article-title>Regulated nuclear translocation of the Mig1 glucose repressor</article-title>. <source>Mol Biol Cell</source> <volume>8</volume>: <fpage>1603</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1618</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9285828</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Dodou</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Treisman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name> (<year>1997</year>) <article-title>The Saccharomyces cerevisiae MADS-box transcription factor Rlm1 is a target for the Mpk1 mitogen-activated protein kinase pathway</article-title>. <source>Mol Cell Biol</source> <volume>17</volume>: <fpage>1848</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1859</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9121433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Barald</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name> (<year>1991</year>) <article-title>The cellular environment controls the expression of engrailed-like protein in the cranial neuroepithelium of quail-chick chimeric embryos</article-title>. <source>Development (Cambridge, England)</source> <volume>113</volume>: <fpage>1037</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1048</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Gertz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Siggia</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name> (<year>2009</year>) <article-title>Analysis of combinatorial cis-regulation in synthetic and genomic promoters</article-title>. <source>Nature</source> <volume>457</volume>: <fpage>215</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19029883</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Ghaemmaghami</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Huh</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Bower</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Howson</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Belle</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Dephoure</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name>, <name><surname>O'Shea</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Weissman</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name> (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>Global analysis of protein expression in yeast</article-title>. <source>Nature</source> <volume>425</volume>: <fpage>737</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>741</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14562106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Gregori</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Kahn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Pichard</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name> (<year>1993</year>) <article-title>Competition between transcription factors HNF1 and HNF3, and alternative cell-specific activation by DBP and C/EBP contribute to the regulation of the liver-specific aldolase B promoter</article-title>. <source>Nucleic Acids Res</source> <volume>21</volume>: <fpage>897</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>903</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8383844</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Killion</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Iyer</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name> (<year>2007</year>) <article-title>Genetic reconstruction of a functional transcriptional regulatory network</article-title>. <source>Nat Genet</source> <volume>39</volume>: <fpage>683</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>687</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17417638</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Huh</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Falvo</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Gerke</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Carroll</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Howson</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Weissman</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name>, <name><surname>O'Shea</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name> (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>Global analysis of protein localization in budding yeast</article-title>. <source>Nature</source> <volume>425</volume>: <fpage>686</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>691</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14562095</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Polish</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name> (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>Specificity and regulation of DNA binding by the yeast glucose transporter gene repressor Rgt1</article-title>. <source>Mol Cell Biol</source> <volume>23</volume>: <fpage>5208</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12861007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Kuras</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Barbey</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name> (<year>1997</year>) <article-title>Assembly of a bZIP-bHLH transcription activation complex: formation of the yeast Cbf1-Met4-Met28 complex is regulated through Met28 stimulation of Cbf1 DNA binding</article-title>. <source>EMBO J</source> <volume>16</volume>: <fpage>2441</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>2451</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9171357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Kwon</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Edenberg</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Hur</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name> (<year>1999</year>) <article-title>Sp3 and Sp4 can repress transcription by competing with Sp1 for the core cis-elements on the human ADH5/FDH minimal promoter</article-title>. <source>J Biol Chem</source> <volume>274</volume>: <fpage>20</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9867805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Liaw</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Brandl</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name> (<year>1994</year>) <article-title>Defining the sequence specificity of the Saccharomyces cerevisiae DNA binding protein REB1p by selecting binding sites from random-sequence oligonucleotides</article-title>. <source>Yeast (Chichester, England)</source> <volume>10</volume>: <fpage>771</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>787</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Lundin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Nehlin</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Ronne</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name> (<year>1994</year>) <article-title>Importance of a flanking AT-rich region in target site recognition by the GC box-binding zinc finger protein MIG1</article-title>. <source>Mol Cell Biol</source> <volume>14</volume>: <fpage>1979</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1985</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8114729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Lutfiyya</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Iyer</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name>, <name><surname>DeRisi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>DeVit</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name> (<year>1998</year>) <article-title>Characterization of three related glucose repressors and genes they regulate in Saccharomyces cerevisiae</article-title>. <source>Genetics</source> <volume>150</volume>: <fpage>1377</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1391</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9832517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Mai</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Breeden</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name> (<year>1997</year>) <article-title>Xbp1, a stress-induced transcriptional repressor of the Saccharomyces cerevisiae Swi4/Mbp1 family</article-title>. <source>Mol Cell Biol</source> <volume>17</volume>: <fpage>6491</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6501</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9343412</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Martinez-Pastor</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Marchler</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Schuller</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Marchler-Bauer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Ruis</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Estruch</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name> (<year>1996</year>) <article-title>The Saccharomyces cerevisiae zinc finger proteins Msn2p and Msn4